sson_name"}, {"content": "A Great Elevator Pitch", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 6, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 3, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.2", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Discuss factual and abstract information about common everyday or job related topics in both work and social contexts appropriate for the interlocutor", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts. Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn10le03ob06re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to get the point", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to understand", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Young man, I am not sure you got the point, but we are currently not hiring.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le03ob06aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use when you ask someone to listen to an elevator pitch.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to graduate from", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to finish a program of study", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Mr. Brody, my name is Adam Bari and I have recently graduated from college with a degree in communications.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le03ob06aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "a degree in ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the area of your studies", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I have recently graduated from college with a degree in communications.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le03ob06aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "pressed for time", "type": "name"}, {"content": "busy; hurried", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I am also a bit pressed for time. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le03ob06aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "a hectic schedule", "type": "name"}, {"content": " many things to do", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I realized that you have a hectic schedule Mr. Brody.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le03ob06aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to enable", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to allow; to permit", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: My diverse skills enable me to make a valuable contribution to your company. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le03ob06aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "valuable contributions", "type": "name"}, {"content": "something that is done or given that helps the team or company a lot", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I can make a valuable contribution to your company.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le03ob06aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "professional writing", "type": "name"}, {"content": "writing for a specific profession", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: While being new to professional writing, I have been published in 5 medium-circulation publications.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le03ob06aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "circulation", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the number of copies of each edition of a newspaper that are printed", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Adam has been published in 5 medium-circulation publications over the last year. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le03ob06aud09", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to have a knack for", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to be good at", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I have a knack for making communications materials that are highly readable.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le03ob06aud10", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Let's Contrast: Simple Present, Present Continuous, Simple Past and Present Perfect", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use different tenses to refer to different time frames. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You use the <span class=\"strong\">Simple Present</span> tense to talk about:<ol><li>a repeated or usual action</li> <li>  a truth </li> <li> scheduled events in the near future</li> </ol> For example:</br><span class=\"italic\"> I want to take one minute of your time to introduce myself. </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Continuous tense</span> to talk about: <ol><li>actions or events happening NOW </li> <li> temporary actions </li> <li>definite future plans </li> <li> changing situations</li></ol> For example: </br><span class=\"italic\"> I am not sure you got the point, but <span class=\"underline\">we are currently not hiring</span>.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use the <span class=\"strong\">Simple Past tense</span> to talk about:<ol> <li> finished events or actions in the past </li> <li> several finished events in the past (a list)</li> <li> duration of a past event </li></ol> For example: </br><span class=\"italic\"> After chatting with your secretary, I <span class=\"underline\">realized that</span> you have a hectic schedule, Mr. Brody. </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": " You use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect tense</span> to talk about:  <ol><li>an action that happened at an unspecified time in the past </li> <li> past experiences</li> <li>  accomplishments </li> </ol> For example:  </br><span class=\"italic\">My name is Adam Bari and I <span class=\"underline\">have</span> recently <span class=\"underline\">graduated</span> from college with a degree in communications.</span>", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Expressing Time: <span class=\"italic\">-ing</span> Clauses", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " You can use -ing clauses to express time.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "A clause is a part of a sentence with its own subject and verb. You can use verb+ing in a clause to refer to when something happens.</br></br>  For example: </br></br><span class=\"italic\"> Chatting with your secretary, I realized that you have a hectic schedule, Mr. Brody. </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can also use an <span class=\"italic\">-ing</span> form after <span class=\"italic\">ever since</span>, <span class=\"italic\">since</span>, <span class=\"italic\">after</span>, <span class=\"italic\">before</span>, <span class=\"italic\">while</span>, <span class=\"italic\">when</span>, <span class=\"italic\">whenever</span>.</br></br>  For example:</br></br><span class=\"italic\">  Before starting, I have to tell you that you've got 60 seconds and I hope you don't waste my time. </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "While <span class=\"strong\">completing my studies</span>, I worked on the college newspaper as a reporter, and eventually, as the editor of the art section. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "While <span class=\"strong\">being</span> new to professional writing, I have been published in 5 medium-circulation publications over the last year.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I read an elevator pitch.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I give feedback on an elevator pitch (positive and negative).", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write a new and improved elevator pitch.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Find a partner who prepared an elevator pitch for the last lesson, or find an elevator pitch online.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Decide what you like and don't like about it. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Prepare a T-chart. Draw a large T on a page of paper. On the left side of the T, put the things you like about the pitch. On the right side, put the things you don't like.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write a new and improved pitch for the same person.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read the new pitch aloud.", "type": "text"}]}]}